=== NAME  TestE1v2_ThreeModelComparison
    e1_models_test.go:352: 
    e1_models_test.go:353: VERDICT (refutation-first):
    e1_models_test.go:354:  1. Concurrency safety (M1) is a property of LOCKING: with equal mutexes, every
    e1_models_test.go:355:     model preserves monotonic counters. The register file adds nothing here.
    e1_models_test.go:356:  2. Invariant enforcement (M2) is a property of the CLOSED, POLICY-GUARDED SURFACE:
    e1_models_test.go:357:     A (map) and B (plain struct) admit invalid states (wrong types, out-of-domain
    e1_models_test.go:358:     values, regressions); B′ (guarded struct) and C (registers) repel them all.
    e1_models_test.go:359:  3. B′ matches C on every measured property (M1, M1b, M2, M3, auditability). The
    e1_models_test.go:360:     register abstraction is NOT proven necessary by E1v2 — the load-bearing
    e1_models_test.go:361:     property is the guarded surface. Necessity is tested component-by-component in
    e1_models_test.go:362:     E0; the remaining case for $R0$–$R7$ rests on notation, audit-by-construction
    e1_models_test.go:363:     and the hardware metaphor, not on these metrics.
